WEBVTT

00:00.917 --> 00:02.460
In the year 845,

00:03.169 --> 00:08.800
the Colossal Titan
and the Armored Titan suddenly appeared.

00:09.426 --> 00:12.887
They destroyed one of humanity's walls
and everyday life with it.

00:15.974 --> 00:18.309
Humanity abandoned Wall Maria,

00:18.893 --> 00:22.313
lost twenty percent of its population
and a third of its territory,

00:23.022 --> 00:26.818
and was forced to
retreat behind Wall Rose.

00:29.487 --> 00:31.072
In the year 850,

00:32.073 --> 00:36.578
the Colossal Titan reappeared
and demolished another wall.

00:36.661 --> 00:40.749
Once again, humanity allowed
the Titans to further their advance.

00:41.374 --> 00:44.794
One after another,
soldiers fell to the Titans.

00:45.670 --> 00:46.880
And then...

00:46.963 --> 00:48.173
Eren!

00:48.715 --> 00:49.924
Hurry!

00:53.386 --> 00:57.223
Eren Jaeger, who had fallen prey to one

01:00.769 --> 01:05.273
reappeared from inside a mysterious Titan.

01:07.233 --> 01:09.694
Attention!

01:11.112 --> 01:14.908
Dot Pyxis, the top officer in charge
of the entire southern territory,

01:14.991 --> 01:19.412
took notice of Eren Jaeger's
strength while fighting in Titan form

01:19.496 --> 01:22.874
and decided to carry out an unusual plan.

01:23.708 --> 01:27.003
In Titan form, he will lift
that giant rock near the front gate,

01:27.086 --> 01:30.048
carry it to the wrecked gate,
and seal the hole!

01:31.674 --> 01:33.760
Should this operation succeed,

01:33.843 --> 01:38.890
we could take back the land
that the Titans have taken away from us!

01:40.266 --> 01:42.936
For mankind, that single, small step

01:43.019 --> 01:45.146
could be a big leap forward!

01:48.525 --> 01:53.488
However, that plan was on
the verge of failure as soon as it began.

03:35.757 --> 03:38.343
We've successfully managed to gather

03:38.426 --> 03:40.845
most of the Titans
into the corner of the city.

03:40.929 --> 03:43.848
Yet despite avoiding combat
as much as possible,

03:43.932 --> 03:46.309
around 20 percent of our soldier
lost their lives.

03:47.560 --> 03:49.646
No, they didn't lose their lives.

03:49.979 --> 03:52.649
The soldiers did not die
of their own accord.

03:55.068 --> 03:57.612
I ordered them to their deaths.

03:59.447 --> 04:02.075
Humanity is now perched
on the brink of extinction.

04:02.659 --> 04:05.370
If it means ensuring mankind's survival,

04:05.995 --> 04:08.915
I'm willing to go down
in history as a butcher.

04:26.266 --> 04:27.350
Ackermann!

04:39.904 --> 04:41.823
Hey! Stop, Ackermann!

04:41.906 --> 04:43.491
Get away from him!

04:43.574 --> 04:46.119
Eren! Don't you recognize me?

04:46.202 --> 04:47.453
I'm Mikasa!

04:47.537 --> 04:49.956
Part of your family!

04:50.415 --> 04:53.501
You have to seal the hole with that rock!

04:54.377 --> 04:56.129
The operation is a failure.

04:56.713 --> 05:00.883
I knew there was no secret weapon.

05:06.180 --> 05:08.308
Eren, you're a human!

05:08.391 --> 05:09.809
Remember!

05:09.892 --> 05:11.227
Dodge, Ackermann!

05:26.284 --> 05:27.493
What the hell?

05:27.869 --> 05:30.246
He's just a regular, dumb Titan!

05:30.330 --> 05:31.956
- Eren!
- Captain Ian!

05:32.540 --> 05:34.375
Two Titans are up ahead!

05:34.459 --> 05:36.878
A ten-meter Titan and a six-meter Titan
are approaching.

05:36.961 --> 05:41.007
Another 12-meter Titan
is closing in from the rear!

05:43.551 --> 05:44.927
Ian! We have to withdraw!

05:45.011 --> 05:48.389
There's no way that kid can seal the hole!

05:48.473 --> 05:52.310
Agreed. We have no choice,
but to leave him here.

05:59.984 --> 06:02.820
Red smoke shell from the Elite Squad!

06:02.904 --> 06:06.824
It seems the mission to seal
the hole has hit a serious snag.

06:07.533 --> 06:08.951
It was all for nothing.

06:09.035 --> 06:11.829
Our friends have died for nothing!

06:14.999 --> 06:16.709
Hey, look over there!

06:16.793 --> 06:18.419
What is it? What's wrong?

06:19.128 --> 06:21.422
They've failed?

06:21.506 --> 06:23.049
How?

06:27.970 --> 06:30.139
Hey! Where are you going, Armin?

06:30.681 --> 06:32.183
Commander Pyxis.

06:32.266 --> 06:35.561
We should go back
to defending the gate immediately.

06:35.645 --> 06:36.854
Just give the word, sir.

06:36.938 --> 06:38.231
No.

06:38.648 --> 06:40.691
Shall I order the Elite Squad to withdraw?

06:40.775 --> 06:41.859
No.

06:41.943 --> 06:45.113
Continue to lure the
Titans into the corner of town.

06:46.322 --> 06:50.326
As for the Elite Squad, I've left all
on-site decision-making in their hands.

06:50.409 --> 06:52.912
They're more than just skilled.

06:52.995 --> 06:56.707
They're the best of the best, with
the fate of mankind on their shoulders.

06:57.625 --> 07:01.254
Admitting defeat so easily
is not an option.

07:01.337 --> 07:04.882
If we don't want
our fallen soldiers' deaths to be in vain,

07:05.716 --> 07:09.303
then we must struggle
for as long as we live.

07:10.221 --> 07:13.307
Hey! This is no time
to hesitate! Make the call!

07:13.391 --> 07:15.726
Ian! It isn't your fault!

07:15.810 --> 07:18.104
This whole mission
was a long shot to begin with!

07:18.187 --> 07:19.647
We all understand!

07:19.730 --> 07:23.234
It was worth a shot,
and we did the best that we could!

07:23.651 --> 07:26.988
So our teams are
going back up the wall now!

07:29.699 --> 07:31.159
Wait!

07:31.242 --> 07:33.619
Wait. Calm down, Ackermann.

07:34.036 --> 07:36.831
Rico Team, take out
the 12-meter one to the rear!

07:37.790 --> 07:40.001
Mitabi Team and my team
will deal with the two ahead!

07:40.084 --> 07:41.252
What?

07:41.335 --> 07:43.171
I was the one put in charge!

07:43.254 --> 07:45.256
Do as you're ordered!

07:45.673 --> 07:48.843
We can't leave Jaeger defenseless!

07:49.927 --> 07:51.429
Change of plans!

07:51.512 --> 07:54.974
We must protect Jaeger from
the other Titans until we can recover him!

07:55.558 --> 07:57.977
He is the humanity's hope.

07:58.352 --> 08:00.438
We can't abandon him just like that!

08:01.189 --> 08:04.901
Because unlike us, he can't be replaced.

08:05.443 --> 08:07.945
Hundreds of people have died
in this mission alone

08:08.029 --> 08:10.698
for that failure of a human weapon!

08:10.781 --> 08:12.158
Yet you want to recover him

08:12.366 --> 08:14.285
and go through the same thing
all over again?

08:14.619 --> 08:15.912
That's right.

08:15.995 --> 08:19.290
We have to keep trying,
no matter how many people die!

08:25.838 --> 08:28.049
What happened with Eren?

08:28.132 --> 08:30.134
Armin is on his way there.

08:30.593 --> 08:32.762
It will be all right, I think.

08:32.845 --> 08:34.055
You think?

08:34.138 --> 08:36.474
I'm sure everything will be fine.

08:36.557 --> 08:38.643
- Eren will pull through for us!
- Yes.

08:39.519 --> 08:41.979
Gathering the Titans in the corner of town

08:42.063 --> 08:43.814
seems nothing but pointless to me.

08:43.898 --> 08:47.610
A fight against a Titan
always turns into a battle of attrition.

08:47.693 --> 08:50.696
We need to avoid losing men
at this point in time.

08:52.990 --> 08:56.244
Meaning soldiers who die at this point
in time are dying for nothing?

08:56.661 --> 08:58.579
We'll wage war someday!

08:58.663 --> 09:01.332
So it makes sense to minimize our losses
and conserve our manpower

09:01.415 --> 09:03.626
until that time comes!

09:04.252 --> 09:07.046
- This is the right call to make!
- Is it really though?

09:07.129 --> 09:08.214
It is!

09:09.048 --> 09:12.385
Well, let's just try
not to end up being "losses."

09:12.468 --> 09:13.928
Both of us.

09:14.762 --> 09:16.430
Are you serious, Ian?

09:16.514 --> 09:19.433
How is humanity
ever going to beat the Titans then?

09:19.517 --> 09:21.227
Tell me, Rico!

09:21.310 --> 09:24.438
What other way do we have
of putting an end to all this?

09:24.522 --> 09:27.900
How can we defeat
the overwhelming might of the Titans

09:27.984 --> 09:31.779
while maintaining our humanity
and not letting anyone die?

09:32.530 --> 09:36.325
I have no idea
how to defeat the Titans, obviously.

09:37.493 --> 09:38.536
Yes.

09:38.661 --> 09:42.206
That's why we must do this now.
It's our only option.

09:42.790 --> 09:45.626
We have to lay down
our lives and go down bravely

09:46.669 --> 09:50.006
for this so-called human weapon
we barely know anything about!

09:51.340 --> 09:52.550
It's pathetic, isn't it?

09:53.175 --> 09:56.512
That this is all we humans can do.

09:57.597 --> 09:59.807
So what do you say?

10:00.516 --> 10:02.643
This is our battle to wage.

10:03.644 --> 10:05.479
Our chance to struggle!

10:16.073 --> 10:18.326
I refuse.

10:18.659 --> 10:19.702
Rico!

10:20.536 --> 10:22.163
I'll follow your plan.

10:23.331 --> 10:25.750
I think your assessment is right.

10:26.334 --> 10:28.169
I'm going to fight with all my might

10:28.252 --> 10:30.838
and make them taste
the ferocity of mankind.

10:31.589 --> 10:33.591
Because I refuse to die for nothing.

10:34.300 --> 10:37.845
My team will handle
the 12-meter one to the rear.

10:41.349 --> 10:44.226
Let's go! We have the two in front!

10:44.310 --> 10:45.186
Yes.

10:48.189 --> 10:51.025
Thank you, Captain Ian.

10:51.108 --> 10:53.402
There's no need to thank me, Ackermann.

10:54.362 --> 10:57.823
You scared me. Since there
was no telling what you might do next.

10:58.699 --> 11:00.993
Now you can move freely
and act as originally planned.

11:01.077 --> 11:03.371
That should make
better use of your ability.

11:03.954 --> 11:04.789
Yes, sir.

11:05.665 --> 11:07.375
This is to protect your lover, after all.

11:08.125 --> 11:09.794
He's family.

11:15.883 --> 11:16.967
What?

11:17.676 --> 11:19.929
The damaged parts haven't repaired?

11:20.554 --> 11:22.181
Is it because of his earlier wounds?

11:24.558 --> 11:26.560
How is it affecting Eren?

11:26.644 --> 11:30.648
In fact, what guarantee is there
that he can turn back to normal at all?

11:31.899 --> 11:33.317
No, never mind.

11:33.401 --> 11:35.569
I won't figure out anything
just by thinking.

11:36.112 --> 11:39.990
For now, I have to do what I can!

11:47.957 --> 11:48.999
Eren.

11:49.083 --> 11:50.209
Mikasa.

11:50.292 --> 11:51.961
What happened?

12:09.937 --> 12:11.272
What?

12:11.355 --> 12:13.357
What...

12:14.024 --> 12:16.610
am I doing now?

12:17.736 --> 12:19.280
Am I sitting?

12:19.947 --> 12:21.490
I can't see anything.

12:22.700 --> 12:24.160
What day is today?

12:25.578 --> 12:27.455
Where am I?

12:33.335 --> 12:34.420
I see.

12:35.296 --> 12:36.464
I'm at home.

12:43.971 --> 12:45.181
I'm going to sleep.

12:52.855 --> 12:54.064
Eren.

12:55.399 --> 12:58.152
What are you doing, Eren?

12:59.195 --> 13:00.237
Listen up!

13:00.321 --> 13:04.366
We can't let any Titans leave
this corner of town, no matter what!

13:04.450 --> 13:07.495
Focus on that and keep luring them!

13:07.578 --> 13:11.332
You don't need to fight them!
Is that clear?

13:11.415 --> 13:15.002
You'll run along the ground,
three cadets per team.

13:15.085 --> 13:16.962
When you reach the wall, you leap back up.

13:17.046 --> 13:18.672
Don't die out there.

13:18.756 --> 13:21.342
If by some slim chance
a Titan goes astray, we'll take it out.

13:22.468 --> 13:23.969
"By some slim chance"?

13:24.053 --> 13:26.597
There's a pretty good chance,
if you ask me.

13:26.680 --> 13:28.807
If we sense any risk,

13:28.891 --> 13:31.268
are we free to act at our own discretion?

13:31.352 --> 13:33.187
If it will help somehow.

13:36.023 --> 13:37.608
Kirschtein Team, move out!

13:37.691 --> 13:39.026
Yes, sir!

13:57.753 --> 13:59.213
Crap! Behind us!

14:00.381 --> 14:02.007
One 13-meter Titan!

14:02.091 --> 14:03.884
It's headed straight for Jaeger!

14:04.426 --> 14:07.179
We have more Titans
coming through the gate!

14:07.930 --> 14:09.932
Four of them are all around
ten meters high!

14:10.015 --> 14:13.102
- Ackermann! You have the rear one!
- Understood!

14:13.185 --> 14:14.937
Don't let it get to Jaeger!

14:15.521 --> 14:17.648
- Let's hold them off here!
- Understood!

14:17.982 --> 14:21.443
Elite soldiers or not, two teams
can't handle four Titans at once.

14:37.126 --> 14:38.377
This can't be.

14:38.460 --> 14:40.588
Why are there so many Titans

14:41.422 --> 14:43.257
even though there are so few people here?

14:43.799 --> 14:47.094
Wait, could it be that Eren
is drawing them in?

14:47.177 --> 14:48.262
Mikasa!

14:49.054 --> 14:50.514
What happened to the plan?

14:50.598 --> 14:51.599
Armin!

14:51.682 --> 14:53.267
What happened to Eren?

14:53.350 --> 14:55.436
Get away! It's dangerous there!

14:55.519 --> 14:58.272
That Titan isn't acting
through Eren's will!

14:58.814 --> 15:01.066
I called out to him,
but he wouldn't respond!

15:01.150 --> 15:03.319
There's no getting through to him anymore!

15:03.402 --> 15:04.570
What about the plan?

15:04.653 --> 15:05.946
It has failed!

15:06.030 --> 15:09.033
We're fighting
because we can't leave Eren behind!

15:09.116 --> 15:11.160
But there are too many Titans here.

15:11.243 --> 15:13.245
At this rate,
we'll eventually be wiped out!

15:25.049 --> 15:27.176
From the back of the head to the nape,

15:27.843 --> 15:31.138
one meter high and ten centimeters across!

15:31.597 --> 15:32.598
Armin!

15:32.681 --> 15:34.725
I'll get Eren out of here!

15:34.808 --> 15:37.603
You just protect us from the other Titans!

15:38.479 --> 15:39.939
What are you planning?

15:40.689 --> 15:43.901
Eren came out of the Titans' vital spot!

15:45.235 --> 15:48.238
My guess is that has something to do

15:48.322 --> 15:50.282
with whatever makes the Titans tick.

15:50.783 --> 15:52.034
It's okay.

15:52.117 --> 15:54.119
As long as I miss the center,

15:55.371 --> 15:57.831
he won't die.

15:57.915 --> 15:59.416
It will just

16:00.376 --> 16:02.002
hurt a little bit!

16:02.086 --> 16:03.045
Armin!

16:12.763 --> 16:14.598
Stop, Armin! That's too reckless!

16:14.682 --> 16:15.808
Mikasa!

16:15.891 --> 16:20.145
Just go do what you can!
There are lives you must save!

16:20.229 --> 16:23.023
Leave Eren to me and go!

16:30.322 --> 16:32.324
Eren! Can you hear me?

16:32.408 --> 16:34.118
Pull yourself together!

16:34.201 --> 16:37.037
We're all going to die
if you don't come out of there!

16:37.121 --> 16:39.915
Don't give in to the Titan's body!

16:39.999 --> 16:43.919
Now just hurry
and get out of this lump of flesh!

16:44.795 --> 16:46.422
Get out of here?

16:47.131 --> 16:48.465
Why?

16:49.425 --> 16:51.719
I'm sleepy now.

16:51.802 --> 16:53.262
Eren!

16:53.429 --> 16:55.764
Come out! Hurry!

16:55.848 --> 16:57.933
Eren!

17:02.229 --> 17:05.315
What happened to your plan
to avenge your mother?

17:05.399 --> 17:07.985
You were going to chase out
all the Titans, remember?

17:08.068 --> 17:11.488
You hate them for killing
your mother, remember?

17:12.614 --> 17:14.616
What are you talking about, Armin?

17:16.368 --> 17:18.996
My mom is right here.

17:20.164 --> 17:21.999
Eren!

17:22.082 --> 17:23.917
Wake up, Eren!

17:24.001 --> 17:26.253
You're in there, aren't you? Eren!

17:26.336 --> 17:29.465
If we stay here, the Titans will kill us!

17:29.631 --> 17:31.717
It will all end here!

17:33.802 --> 17:37.598
Seriously, you're not
making any sense, Armin.

17:40.392 --> 17:43.187
Why should I have to go outside?

17:43.520 --> 17:44.605
Right.

17:45.272 --> 17:47.566
Why would I want to leave?

17:51.278 --> 17:53.739
Why would I want to join the Scouts?

18:03.123 --> 18:06.210
Whether we like it or not,
we're on our own now!

18:16.428 --> 18:17.971
Got you!

18:24.520 --> 18:27.022
About time you kicked the bucket, bastard!

18:32.361 --> 18:34.113
Get away for now!

18:34.196 --> 18:35.739
I've returned!

18:35.823 --> 18:37.825
I'll rendezvous with Mitabi Team!

18:47.668 --> 18:49.002
What?

18:54.633 --> 18:55.634
Jean!

18:55.968 --> 18:56.927
Get going!

19:00.973 --> 19:03.934
I've had enough of people dying
because of me!

19:18.949 --> 19:21.326
Damn! Of all the times
to have a malfunction!

19:40.262 --> 19:41.305
Jean!

19:46.518 --> 19:47.978
What's going on?

19:48.562 --> 19:50.564
Why isn't he using
his omnidirectional mobility gear?

19:52.024 --> 19:53.150
Oh, no!

19:53.233 --> 19:55.402
Don't tell me it's malfunctioning?

19:56.320 --> 19:58.405
I'll manage somehow!

20:09.875 --> 20:13.587
Damn. I can't believe
I'm dragging everyone down.

20:27.017 --> 20:30.646
Will this really work out somehow?

20:33.357 --> 20:34.733
Eren.

20:35.484 --> 20:36.860
Eren.

20:37.402 --> 20:38.487
Eren.

20:40.197 --> 20:41.615
Eren.

20:43.116 --> 20:47.287
We're supposed to explore
the outside world someday, remember?

20:50.082 --> 20:53.085
Far beyond these walls,

20:54.086 --> 20:55.379
there stretch fiery waters,

20:55.462 --> 20:56.713
lands of ice,

20:57.631 --> 21:00.175
and sandy snowfields.

21:00.842 --> 21:04.471
The world my mom
and dad planned to venture into.

21:09.184 --> 21:11.436
I thought you'd just forgotten,

21:12.271 --> 21:14.731
but you actually stopped talking about it

21:14.815 --> 21:18.110
because you didn't want me
to join the Scouting Regiment, right?

21:19.278 --> 21:21.613
The outside world?

21:25.534 --> 21:27.869
Eren, answer me.

21:28.370 --> 21:32.749
Even though just one step
outside the wall lies a hellish world

21:33.500 --> 21:38.005
and even though it might mean dying
a gruesome death like my parents,

21:38.588 --> 21:43.343
didn't you want to go
to the outside world?

21:46.430 --> 21:47.889
Why?

21:49.266 --> 21:52.185
Isn't that obvious?

21:54.896 --> 21:56.189
Because

21:56.273 --> 21:58.483
I was born in this world!

23:43.630 --> 23:45.632
Go! Run! Live!

23:46.716 --> 23:51.555
As innumerable words mix and countless
lives are lost on the battlefield,

23:52.222 --> 23:55.976
Eren holds hope aloft
and heads for the gate.
